# Course robot, safety requirements for the arm (hazards H2, H3, H5 of F11-19). Build ids are
# the course's own labels for the lab runs of this build.
RELEASE|ss402-lab-1
R|SG1|1|-|the arm comes to rest after an e-stop before drive power is removed
R|SG2|1|-|the arm joint never exceeds the hazardous speed
R|SG3|1|-|the arm never starts moving by itself after a stop
R|SR1|1|SG1|the hard-wired chain removes drive power within the relay delay after a press
R|SR2|2|SG1|the control thread reads the e-stop input every cycle and ramps the arm to rest
R|SR3|1|SG2|a speed monitor on an independent encoder trips above the limit
R|SR4|2|SG3|a window watchdog trips on missing or early kicks and disables the drive
R|SR5|1|SG3|a trip is latched; reset is refused while the e-stop is pressed; restart from 0
D|D1|SR1|two-channel safety relay with fixed delay, contactors K1 and K2
D|D2|SR2|control loop reads the e-stop input at the start of each cycle
D|D3|SR3|speed monitor on joint-side encoder B
D|D4|SR4|Watchdog class (window 5..50 ms)
D|D5|SR5|Watchdog::kick and Watchdog::reset rules
T|T1|SR1|1|e-stop chain test on the real robot with a timer on the drive enable
T|T2|SR2|2|estop_fixed run (F11-21): at rest before the relay opens
T|T3|SR3|1|safety_function stuck_encoder_A scenario (F11-18)
T|T4|SR4|2|watchdog_test T1 T2 T3 (F11-21)
T|T5|SR5|1|watchdog_test T4 T5 and mutants (F11-21)
X|T2|PASS|ss402-lab-1|F11-21/estop_fixed.out
X|T3|PASS|ss402-lab-1|F11-18/safety_function.out
X|T4|PASS|ss402-lab-1|F11-21/watchdog_test.out
X|T5|PASS|ss402-lab-1|F11-21/watchdog_test.out
